# YouTube Data API v3 (recommended for `npm run fetch-messages`)
# Lists every public video on the channel's Videos tab (long-form playlist: no Shorts, no livestreams).
# Without a key the script still works, but only sees the 15 newest videos and merges them into the catalog.
# Enable "YouTube Data API v3" in Google Cloud Console, then create an API key:
# https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/library/youtube.googleapis.com
#
# Important: for `npm run fetch-messages` on your computer, the key must NOT use "HTTP referrers"
# (website restrictions). Use Application restrictions → None, or IP addresses for a server.
# Otherwise you get 403 "requests ... are blocked".
YOUTUBE_API_KEY=

# Optional: channel (default UC… = @damiolatunji / Herdentity)
# YOUTUBE_CHANNEL_ID=UCyfEw0p5Rx-oGpyex3RWNTw

